{"results":[{"url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/history/2020/10/08/lincoln-supreme-court-kamala-harris/","final_url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/history/2020/10/08/lincoln-supreme-court-kamala-harris/","title":"Kamala Harris’s ‘little history lesson’ about Lincoln’s Supreme Court vacancy wasn’t exactly true","description":"The Democratic candidate claimed in a debate with Vice President Mike Pence Wednesday night that Abraham Lincoln delayed his Supreme Court pick in 1864 so the American people could \"make the decision.\"","language":"en","text":"Democracy Dies in Darkness\n\nBy  Gillian Brockell\n\nThe question from vice-presidential debate moderator Susan Page was actually about preexisting conditions.\n\nBut Vice President Pence ignored it because he wanted to raise the specter of Democrats packing the Supreme Court if former vice president Joe Biden and California Sen. Kamala D. Harris win the election next month.\n\n---","author":"Gillian Brockell","published_date":"2020-10-09T00:13:16.728Z","latency_ms":1607.7831879993028,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}